SUSFS v2.4.0 uses SUSFS_LOGI_RL() unconditionally in fs/susfs.c, but
defines the ratelimited logging macros only when
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_ENABLE_LOG is enabled.  With logging disabled (the Zyomi16
configuration) the two call sites fail with -Wimplicit-function-declaration.

This is an upstream compatibility fix, not a change to patch 50.  It supplies
guarded no-op definitions when the logging-enabled branch did not define the
macros, so the build keeps CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_ENABLE_LOG=n without redefining
anything when logging is enabled.

--- a/fs/susfs.c
+++ b/fs/susfs.c
@@ -50,2 +50,9 @@
+#ifndef SUSFS_LOGI_RL
+#define SUSFS_LOGI_RL(fmt, ...)
+#endif
+#ifndef SUSFS_LOGE_RL
+#define SUSFS_LOGE_RL(fmt, ...)
+#endif
+
 /* selinux hide */
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(susfs_mutex_lock_sus_type);
